.TH LOV.LAYOUT_PATTERN_TYPES 4 2026-11-10 "Lustre" "Lustre Kernel Interfaces"
.SH NAME
lov.layout_pattern_types \- layout pattern types negotiated with the MDS
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY
.RI "lctl get_param lov." FSNAME -clilov-*.layout_pattern_types
.YS
.SS PROPERTIES
.TP
.B Access Permissions
.br
.BR 444 " | " -r--r--r--
.TP
.B Scope
.br
Per-client LOV device.
.TP
.B Config
.br
.B layout_pattern_types
is always present for client LOV devices.
.TP
.B Default
.br
.RB layout_pattern_types= raid0,mdt,overstriped,hole,released
.SH DESCRIPTION
The comma-separated list of file layout pattern types that this client and
the MDS agreed on when the client connected, which is the intersection of
the types the client sent and the types the MDS advertised in
.BR mdt.layout_pattern_types (4).
On a filesystem with several MDTs the list is the one MDT0000 advertised.
The client only uses layout types in this list: a component with any other
pattern is left uninitialized, and IO reads another mirror instead if the
file has one.
.PP
A client that connects without requesting layout negotiation does not
receive a list, and reports the pre-2.18 baseline of
.BR raid0 ", " mdt " and " overstriped
with the
.BR hole " and " released
layout flags, which every MDS supports.
.PP
An MDS older than 2.18.0 does not know about this field and so cannot
filter the list, and the client keeps the types it asked for.  The answer
is still accurate, because such an MDS offers layout negotiation at all
only when erasure coding is enabled on it, and a client that is not offered
negotiation falls back to the baseline above.
So
.B parity
in this list means that both ends support erasure coded FLR mirrors,
see
.BR lfs-mirror-create (1).
.SH MODULES
This parameter is in the following modules:
.EX
.B lov.*.layout_pattern_types
.EE
.SH CAVEATS
The list is renegotiated whenever the client reconnects to the MDS, so a
change to
.BR mdt.layout_pattern_types (4)
or an MDS upgrade takes effect on the next reconnect.  Files whose layout
the client already holds keep the previous list until their layout lock is
dropped.  The client's own
.BR lustre.enable_flr_ec (4)
setting is read when the filesystem is mounted.
.SH EXAMPLES
Check whether this client negotiated EC layouts:
.EX
.RB "client# " "lctl get_param -n lov.testfs-clilov-*.layout_pattern_types"
raid0,parity,mdt,overstriped,hole,released
.EE
.SH AVAILABILITY
The
.B layout_pattern_types
parameter is part of the
.BR lustre (7)
filesystem package since release 2.18.0.
.\" Added in commit v2_17_60
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR lfs-mirror-create (1),
.BR lustre.enable_flr_ec (4),
.BR mdt.layout_pattern_types (4),
.BR lctl-get_param (8)
